  <div class="block-title"><h3>Under the floor</h3><span class="label">How a call request travels</span></div>
  <div class="eng">
    <div class="eng-diagram">
      <div class="dg">
        <div class="dg-leg"><span class="br"><i></i>Browser</span><span class="sv"><i></i>Server route</span><span class="ml"><i></i>Email</span><em>No database anywhere in this path</em></div>
        <ol class="dg-nodes">
          <li class="br" style="--i:0"><span>01 · Browser</span><b>detectTimezone()</b><p>Reads the visitor's zone from the browser. The draft lives in session storage.</p></li>
          <li class="sv" style="--i:1"><span>02 · GET availability</span><b>config</b><p>Mon–Fri 09:00–18:00 Austin time, 30 min, 4 h notice, 14 days.</p></li>
          <li class="sv" style="--i:2"><span>03 · Server</span><b>generateSlots()</b><p>Wall clock to UTC with a two-pass offset lookup.</p></li>
          <li class="br" style="--i:3"><span>04 · Browser</span><b>groupByDay()</b><p>Formats each instant in the visitor's zone, grouped by local day.</p></li>
          <li class="sv" style="--i:4"><span>05 · POST requests</span><b>validate</b><p>Honeypot first, then field checks. Bad input returns 422.</p></li>
          <li class="sv" style="--i:5"><span>06 · Server</span><b>race guard</b><p>Regenerates the slots. A stale or taken pick returns 409.</p></li>
          <li class="sv" style="--i:6"><span>07 · Server</span><b>buildIcs()</b><p>RFC 5545 text, METHOD:REQUEST, STATUS:TENTATIVE, stable UID.</p></li>
          <li class="ml" style="--i:7"><span>08 · SMTP</span><b>owner, then visitor</b><p>The visitor copy is sent only if the owner email went out. Otherwise 502.</p></li>
        </ol>
        <div class="dg-trace"><span class="tag">One slot, four spellings</span>
          <div><code>09:00 America/Chicago</code><i>→</i><code class="hi">2027-03-15T14:00:00Z</code><i>→</i><code>15:00 Europe/Madrid</code><i>→</i><code>DTSTART:20270315T140000Z</code></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="eng-notes">
      <div><h4>Time zones without a library</h4><p>To turn "9:00 in Austin" into an exact instant, the generator guesses, asks the browser's date formatter what the Austin offset is at that guess, corrects, then asks once more. The second pass catches the days when clocks change. Six unit tests pin the behaviour.</p></div>
      <div><h4>Booking with no database</h4><p>The server never trusts the slot the browser sends. It regenerates the list at submit time and rejects anything missing with a 409, which also covers expired slots. The email to the studio is the record, so the visitor is only told "request received" after that email has actually been sent.</p></div>
      <div><h4>A calendar invite written by hand</h4><p>The .ics attachment is about 20 lines of plain text assembled by a pure function: UTC start and end, a stable ID derived from the request, and escaping for commas, semicolons and line breaks. It adds no dependency and is covered by its own tests.</p></div>
      <div><h4>Motion on a budget</h4><p>The particle count is one per 2,400 square pixels, capped at 750 and cut to 220 on phones, with pixel density capped at 1.5. Every canvas stops when it leaves the screen or the tab is hidden, and none of them start for visitors who ask for reduced motion.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>

